WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.037
Normalization separates facts into different tables
so

00:00:03.063 --> 00:00:06.658
each fact has a clear home Later

00:00:06.843 --> 00:00:10.014
analytical queries reconnect those tables through
keys

00:00:11.751 --> 00:00:13.711
This slide previews that idea with a

00:00:13.724 --> 00:00:16.937
provided join query Joins are taught step

00:00:16.951 --> 00:00:18.898
by step in Module 6 so you

00:00:18.911 --> 00:00:20.595
are not expected to write this query

00:00:20.622 --> 00:00:24.487
yet Run it and inspect the connected

00:00:24.514 --> 00:00:29.871
result Notice how patient provider appointment
service

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:32.516
and service-line information can be combined without

00:00:32.542 --> 00:00:34.226
having stored all of those facts in

00:00:34.253 --> 00:00:37.812
one giant table That is a major

00:00:37.838 --> 00:00:40.522
benefit of relational design store facts in

00:00:40.549 --> 00:00:43.062
well-structured places then reconnect them when a

00:00:43.088 --> 00:00:47.089
question requires a broader view For now

00:00:47.352 --> 00:00:49.536
focus on recognizing how keys make that

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:50.786
reconnection possible
